From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add SHA-256-Indication from 3GPP TS 29.109
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3GPP TS 29.109 V19.0.0 defines this AVP in vendor 10415, which the
dictionary has no entry for at its code:

  SHA-256-Indication (421): Enumerated, 2 values, clause 6.3.1.22

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
index 56a8586..8fc76c2 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
@@ -3023,6 +3023,11 @@
 		<avp name="Security-Feature-Response" code="420" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
 			<type type-name="OctetString"/>
 		</avp>
+		<avp name="SHA-256-Indication" code="421" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Enumerated"/>
+			<enum name="UICC_NOT_SUPPORT_SHA256" code="0"/>
+			<enum name="UICC_SUPPORT_SHA256" code="1"/>
+		</avp>
 		<avp name="TGPP-Service-Selection" code="493" mandatory="must" protected="mustnot" vendor-bit="mustnot" vendor-id="TGPP">
 			<type type-name="OctetString"/>
 		</avp>
